---
/** StepCards — Figma node 4:62 */
---

<section class="bg-white w-full">
  <div class="max-w-[1232px] mx-auto px-8 pt-32 pb-20 sm:pt-40 sm:pb-28 lg:pt-48 lg:pb-32">
    <!-- Section label -->
    <p class="uppercase text-sm font-medium tracking-[2px] text-dark">
      How it works
    </p>

    <!-- Yellow divider -->
    <div class="w-12 h-0.5 bg-accent mt-4"></div>

    <!-- Two-column layout -->
    <div class="flex flex-row gap-12 mt-12">
      <!-- Left column (~50%) -->
      <div class="w-1/2">
        <!-- Large heading -->
        <h2 data-reveal class="font-heading font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.025em] text-dark" style="font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);">
          One system. One call. One person.
        </h2>

        <!-- Body text -->
        <p data-reveal="fade" style="--reveal-delay: 200ms;" class="text-base text-gray-text mt-4">
          Most pub and restaurant owners are running two separate systems that are supposed to work together but often don't. I replace that with a single, fully integrated solution. Till, card processing, and connectivity, installed, supported, and managed by me.
        </p>

        <!-- Accordion items -->
        <div class="mt-8 flex flex-col">
          <!-- Item 1 (default open) -->
          <div class="border-b-2 border-accent" data-accordion-item data-open="true">
            <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between py-5" data-accordion-trigger>
              <span class="font-heading font-medium text-lg tracking-[-0.5px] text-dark">We talk</span>
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div data-accordion-content>
              <p class="text-[22px] leading-[38.5px] text-dark pb-5">
                You tell me what you've got, what's driving you mad, and what you actually need. No pitch. No pressure. Just a straight conversation, free, with no commitment.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Item 2 (collapsed) -->
          <div class="border-b-2 border-accent" data-accordion-item data-open="false">
            <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between py-5" data-accordion-trigger>
              <span class="font-heading font-medium text-lg tracking-[-0.5px] text-dark">I review your setup</span>
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div data-accordion-content>
              <p class="text-[22px] leading-[38.5px] text-dark pb-5">
                I look at your EPOS, your card processing rates, your connectivity. I tell you honestly what's working, what isn't, and what it's costing you. Most businesses I review are overpaying by 20 to 40 percent on card processing alone.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Item 3 (collapsed) -->
          <div class="border-b-2 border-accent" data-accordion-item data-open="false">
            <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between py-5" data-accordion-trigger>
              <span class="font-heading font-medium text-lg tracking-[-0.5px] text-dark">I build the right solution</span>
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div data-accordion-content>
              <p class="text-[22px] leading-[38.5px] text-dark pb-5">
                Where possible, I implement systems where the card reader is physically integrated into the till. No separate machine, no wifi link to drop, no finger-pointing when something goes wrong. I work with providers I've used in my own businesses and trust completely.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Item 4 (collapsed) -->
          <div class="border-b-2 border-accent" data-accordion-item data-open="false">
            <button class="w-full flex items-center justify-between py-5" data-accordion-trigger>
              <span class="font-heading font-medium text-lg tracking-[-0.5px] text-dark">I stick around</span>
              <svg class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
                <path d="M4 6l4 4 4-4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
              </svg>
            </button>
            <div data-accordion-content>
              <p class="text-[22px] leading-[38.5px] text-dark pb-5">
                This isn't a sale. It's an ongoing relationship. You get one number, mine, for everything. EPOS question? Call me. Card processing issue? Call me. Wifi down? Call me.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Right column (~50%): navy image placeholder -->
      <div class="w-1/2" data-reveal="fade" style="--reveal-delay: 200ms;">
        <div class="bg-navy rounded-lg overflow-hidden aspect-[3/4] flex items-center justify-center p-8">
          <img src={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/images/credo/step-devices.webp`} alt="POS and card machine devices" width="705" height="591" loading="lazy" class="max-w-full max-h-full object-contain" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
